From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cappy Ishihara <cappy@fyralabs.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm: sunxi: commit DSI enabled state after initialization

The DSI atomic-enable path set dsi->enable before clock, PHY, panel, and
output initialization completed. If clock setup failed, the function could
return with dsi->enable still true. A subsequent modeset, output re-add, or
resume then took the already-enabled VRR path and skipped full DSI setup.

Keep the state false until the complete enable sequence has run. This makes
failed or partial enables retryable and applies equally to output hotplug,
suspend/resume, and warm handoff.

--- a/drivers/drm/sunxi_drm_dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/drm/sunxi_drm_dsi.c
@@ -817,7 +817,6 @@
 			DRM_ERROR("Couldn't request the IRQ for dsi\n");
 		}
 	}
-	dsi->enable = true;
 
 	if (dsi->dsi_para.mode_flags & MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO_BURST)
 		dsi->dsi_para.timings.pixel_clk = dsi->dsi_para.timings.pixel_clk * 10 / 9;
@@ -901,6 +900,8 @@
 		dsi->pending_enable_vblank = false;
 	}
 	drm_panel_enable(dsi->sdrm.panel);
+	dsi->enable = true;
+
 	if (dsi->te_gpio)
 		esd_watchdog_start(dsi->esd_wdt);
 	DRM_INFO("[DSI] %s finish\n", __FUNCTION__);
